    {"time":21584,"content":"● Yes. Each open/close of the settings dialog leaks the whole \u001b[36mSettingsDialog\u001b[0m. The last snapshot\r\n"},
    {"time":21984,"content":"  holds 4 closed instances, one per cycle, and the count rose at every step: 240 detached \u001b[36m<div>\u001b[0ms and\r\n"},
    {"time":22116,"content":"  about 875 KB of heap per cycle.\r\n  \r\n"},
    {"time":22500,"content":"  What keeps each dialog alive is its \u001b[36mhandleThemeChange\u001b[0m listener, which is still registered on\r\n"},
    {"time":22764,"content":"  \u001b[36mwindow.eventBus\u001b[0m. Its closure captures the dialog as \u001b[36mthis\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mdialog\u001b[0m:\r\n  \r\n"},
    {"time":23012,"content":"  \u001b[36m@33471 Window / http://localhost:3000 (native)  ← GC root\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":23352,"content":"  \u001b[36m  .global_object → @33803 Window [JSGlobalObject] / http://localhost:3000 (object)\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":23504,"content":"  \u001b[36m  .eventBus → @47965 Object (object)\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":23656,"content":"  \u001b[36m  .listeners → @50799 Array (object)\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":23788,"content":"  \u001b[36m  [3] → @119723 Object (object)\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":23992,"content":"  \u001b[36m  .listener → @121371 handleThemeChange (closure)\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":24244,"content":"  \u001b[36m  .context → @120401 system / Context / scope @65769 (object)\u001b[0m\r\n"},
    {"time":24496,"content":"  \u001b[36m  .this → @120393 SettingsDialog (object)  ← leaked, 787.5 KB\u001b[0m\r\n  \r\n"},
    {"time":24892,"content":"  There is a second reference you have to remove too. The global \u001b[36mopenedDialogs\u001b[0m Set (\u001b[36m.table\u001b[0m → \u001b[36m[i]\u001b[0m)\r\n"},
    {"time":25272,"content":"  still holds each dialog's \u001b[36mDetached\u001b[0m \u001b[36m<div\u001b[0m \u001b[36mclass=\"settings\">\u001b[0m. A scan of every reference into the\r\n"},
    {"time":25652,"content":"  detached DOM found exactly these two app-side holders: that Set and \u001b[36mSettingsDialog.container\u001b[0m.\r\n  \r\n"},
    {"time":26040,"content":"  Each dialog still has an \u001b[36munsubscribe\u001b[0m closure stored on it, so the close path apparently never\r\n"},
    {"time":26380,"content":"  calls it. The fix: call \u001b[36munsubscribe()\u001b[0m on close and \u001b[36mopenedDialogs.delete(container)\u001b[0m.\r\n  \r\n"},
    {"time":26588,"content":"  What a fix saves, measured on the last snapshot:\r\n"},
    {"time":26976,"content":"  - Removing the dialogs frees 3.1 MB (68% of a 4.5 MB heap), about 787 KB per open/close. 99% of\r\n"},
    {"time":27172,"content":"    that is each dialog's \u001b[36mhistory\u001b[0m array (781 KB).\r\n"},
    {"time":27464,"content":"  - Clearing the Set frees another ~177 KB of detached DOM (1,992 nodes).\r\n"},
    {"time":27788,"content":"  - Together that's ~3.3 MB, which covers almost all of the 3.5 MB the heap grew.\r\n  \r\n"},
    {"time":27836,"content":"  Caveats:\r\n"},
    {"time":28216,"content":"  - There is no settle rung (idle + GC), so this can't yet be told apart from in-flight work. A\r\n"},
    {"time":28548,"content":"    dialog that is closed and still on the bus is very unlikely to be that, though.\r\n"},
    {"time":28668,"content":"  - Only 4 cycles were driven.\r\n"},
    {"time":29068,"content":"  - Both roots are page globals (\u001b[36meventBus\u001b[0m, \u001b[36mopenedDialogs\u001b[0m). Confirm they're your app's and not a test\r\n"},
    {"time":29124,"content":"    harness's.\r\n"}
  ]
